/**
 * @defgroup StEmcSimulatorMaker StEmcSimulatorMaker — BEMC Slow Simulator
 * @{
 *
 * @brief Translates GEANT energy depositions into simulated raw ADC hits for
 *        all four sub-detectors of the STAR Barrel Electromagnetic Calorimeter
 *        (BEMC): towers (BTOW), pre-shower (BPRS), and both SMD planes
 *        (BSMDE, BSMDP).
 *
 * @section overview Physics Overview
 *
 * The STAR Barrel EMC is a lead-scintillator sampling calorimeter covering
 * |η| < 1 and the full azimuth (0–2π).  It consists of four instrumented
 * layers read out by photo-detectors:
 *
 * | Sub-detector | Acronym | Channels | Photo-detector | ADC range |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | Barrel EMC Tower         | BTOW  | 4 800  | PMT | 0–4095 |
 * | Barrel Pre-Shower        | BPRS  | 4 800  | PMT | 0–1023 |
 * | Barrel SMD Eta strips    | BSMDE | 18 000 | wire (MAPD/APD-like) | 0–1023 |
 * | Barrel SMD Phi strips    | BSMDP | 18 000 | wire | 0–1023 |
 *
 * @subsection sampling_fraction Sampling Fraction
 *
 * The sampling fraction SF(η) converts the raw GEANT energy deposit dE (in
 * GeV) in the active scintillator into the energy that would be measured in an
 * ideal, perfectly calibrated detector.  It is parameterised as a quadratic
 * function of pseudo-rapidity |η|:
 *
 *   SF(η) = c₀ + c₁·|η| + c₂·η²
 *
 * Default coefficients by sub-detector:
 *
 * | Detector | c₀       | c₁        | c₂       | Notes |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | BTOW  | 14.365   | −0.512    | 0.668    | dimensionless (×10⁻³ relative to 1 GeV) |
 * | BPRS  | 1.0      | 0.0       | 0.0      | energy in scintillator only |
 * | BSMDE | 118 500  | −32 920   | 31 130   | large coefficients: energy scale in strip units |
 * | BSMDP | 126 000  | −13 950   | 19 710   | |
 *
 * @subsection adc_conversion ADC Conversion (Simple Mode)
 *
 * For the simple (non-PMT) path:
 *
 * @code
 *   ADC_ideal = dE · SF(η) / calib
 *   ADC_noisy = ADC_ideal + Gaus(pedMean, pedRMS)      [non-embedding only]
 *   ADC_final = pedMean + (ADC_noisy − pedMean) · Gaus(calibScale, calibSpread)
 *   ADC_final = clamp(ADC_final, 0, Gaus(maxADC, maxADCSpread))
 * @endcode
 *
 * where `calib` [GeV/ADC] is the per-channel gain constant from the database,
 * `pedMean` [ADC] is the channel pedestal, and `pedRMS` [ADC] is the pedestal
 * noise sigma.
 *
 * After digitisation the reconstructed energy is:
 * @code
 *   energy = (ADC − pedMean) · calib
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection pmt_mode PMT Photostatistics Mode
 *
 * For BTOW and BPRS a more detailed simulation converts the energy deposit
 * into a number of photo-electrons and then propagates them through the PMT
 * dynode chain.
 *
 * **Step 1 — Photo-electron yield:**
 * @code
 *   nPhe_mean = dE · mMipPhotoElectrons / mMipEnergyDeposit
 *   nPhe      = Poisson( nPhe_mean )
 * @endcode
 *
 * MIP references used:
 * | Detector | mMipPhotoElectrons | mMipEnergyDeposit |
 * |---|---|---|
 * | BTOW | 63 phe/MIP | 19.8 MeV |
 * | BPRS |  6 phe/MIP |  2.0 MeV |
 *
 * **Step 2 — Total gain:**
 * @code
 *   totalGain = SF(η) · (mMipEnergyDeposit / mMipPhotoElectrons) / calib
 * @endcode
 * This is the ADC-counts-per-incident-photoelectron.
 *
 * **Step 3 — Dynode cascade (kPrimarySecondaryFullMode / kPrimarySecondaryFastMode):**
 * Handled by StPmtSignal::getAdc().
 *
 * **Step 4 — Calibration smear and clamping:**
 * Same as Simple Mode above.
 *
 * @subsection pmt_dynode PMT Dynode Model (StPmtSignal)
 *
 * Models the HAMAMATSU R6427 PMT with 11 dynodes.  The relative inter-dynode
 * voltage distribution is:
 * @code
 *   mNodeVoltage[] = { 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4 }
 * @endcode
 *
 * The secondary-emission coefficients are derived so that the product of all
 * per-dynode gains equals the approximate PMT gain mPmtGain:
 * @code
 *   voltageProduct = ∏ mNodeVoltage[i]
 *   globalCoeff    = (mPmtGain / voltageProduct)^(1/nDynodes)
 *   mSecondaryCoeff[i] = globalCoeff · mNodeVoltage[i]
 * @endcode
 *
 * Inverted partial gains (used for normalisation):
 * @code
 *   mDynodeGain[0] = 1
 *   mDynodeGain[i] = mDynodeGain[i−1] / mSecondaryCoeff[i−1]
 * @endcode
 *
 * **Full Simulator** — propagates a Poisson cascade through every dynode:
 * @code
 *   for i in 0..10:
 *       nElectrons = Poisson( mSecondaryCoeff[i]·nElectrons + mDynodeNoise )
 *   ADC = mTotalGain · nElectrons · mDynodeGain[11]
 *       + Gaus(mPedestalMean, mPedestalRMS)
 * @endcode
 *
 * **Fast Simulator** — switches to a Gaussian approximation once nElectrons ≥ 100,
 * computing the remaining amplification analytically using pre-computed
 * `mG1[]` and `mDNW[]` arrays.  Statistically consistent with the full
 * simulator up to ~10⁵ photo-electrons.
 *
 * @subsection crosstalk Optical Cross-Talk (BSMDE only)
 *
 * The SMD eta strips exhibit capacitive cross-talk.  The simulation leaks a
 * fraction of the energy of the highest-energy strip in a track into its
 * ±5 neighbours:
 * @code
 *   crossTalk = mCrossTalk · (1 − |etaHigh|)
 *   leakE     = crossTalk · (energy_i − energy_{i+1})
 * @endcode
 * The factor (1 − |η|) ensures zero cross-talk at the barrel edge.  Energy is
 * conserved within the 11-strip window examined per track.
 *
 * @}
 */

